Since this restores ILP32 size types for RV32 (undoing what sounds like an
unintentional regression to LP64-style types on 32-bit RISC-V), could you
point to the commit that introduced the regression this is restoring from?
A Fixes: tag would help reviewers and make backporting to stable
clearer, and it isn't present in this patch as sent.

Also, "restore ILP32 size types" touching POSIX-visible size_t/ssize_t/etc.
typedefs is exactly the kind of change that can silently break ABI-sensitive
code (format string mismatches, struct layout in any code assuming the
previous width) - has this been build-tested across all in-tree RV32
targets (not just espressif's), and did you check for any new -Wformat
warnings introduced/fixed by the type width change?
